From fa3d92453a5dc90a9322de34fbf5a31dc8e68de8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ZhangDM-520 <jixianqiang1540@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 20:01:28 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] feat(animation): windows_drag physics tuning keys

The drag physics feel was compile-time: [animation.windows_drag] exposed
only `physics`, and the elastic sheet always ran with the shipped
constants. Six keys now tune it (defaults = those constants, so behavior
is unchanged out of the box):

  stiffness          36.0    return strength of each sheet point
  damping             6.5    wobble decay
  coupling          100.0    rigidity between neighbouring points
  pointer_response    2.0    how far a motion loads the sheet (0 = rigid)
  max_displacement_px 200.0  excursion cap in logical pixels
  settle_after_pause_s 0.25  stillness gap before the sheet snaps to rest

Out-of-range values clamp to their range with the usual named diagnostic;
the keys apply from the next drag on (a drag already in flight keeps its
tuning). The lattice size, contraction factor, 240 Hz step and settle
thresholds stay fixed: the shader and the frame pacing own them.

Co-authored-by: Copilot <223556219+Copilot@users.noreply.github.com>
